  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E27 · December 22, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/16310006">Farewell Rides, Bourbon Hopes, and Cycling Dreams: A Nostalgic Journey with Adam and Michael</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6MTM3MjU1NDk4LCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--64fc63b16c80b699ff156e24429860f959abe1c8/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJqcGciLCJyZXNpemVfdG9fZmlsbCI6WzI1MCwyNTAseyJjcm9wIjoiY2VudHJlIn1dLCJzYXZlciI6eyJxdWFsaXR5Ijo2MH0sImNvbG91cnNwYWNlIjoic3JnYiJ9LCJwdXIiOiJ2YXJpYXRpb24ifX0=--21f3793904e6ce1806a5a794a691217fceef82c7/Road%20Adventures%20of%20Cycling%20Men%20of%20Leisure%20(Podcast%20Cover).jpg" alt="Episode artwork: Farewell Rides, Bourbon Hopes, and Cycling Dreams" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>The Season Three finale gets nostalgic. Adam and Michael reminisce about Ride the Rockies — a
    cherished Colorado event that ended too soon — and cast a worried eye toward the Bourbon Burn, which may
    face a similar fate. With its charming camp atmosphere and distillery visits, they start planning one
    last hurrah to savor those moments while they can.</p>
    <p>From there they draw parallels between the resurgence of bourbon and whiskey and the shifts happening
    within cycling culture: traditional events may struggle to capture younger riders unless they innovate
    with entertainment and modern amenities. Personal stories from the photography world underline just how
    critical adaptation is.</p>
    <p>They close by celebrating a cyclist-artist known for his bicycle and bird portraits, thank Franklin
    Johnson of BRAG for his support, preview the 2025 BRAG event and early-registration perks for the Men
    and Women of Leisure teams — and sign off Season Three with a humorous rant about self-checkout.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/16310006">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E26 · December 8, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/16238805">Smoked Hams, Sunny Escapes, and Holiday Tales: A Festive Journey with Adam and Michael</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6MTM2MzAzOTI3LCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--409e9e33c6c99714ccfc1a2c6f7768a2633c1a51/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJqcGciLCJyZXNpemVfdG9fZmlsbCI6WzI1MCwyNTAseyJjcm9wIjoiY2VudHJlIn1dLCJzYXZlciI6eyJxdWFsaXR5Ijo2MH0sImNvbG91cnNwYWNlIjoic3JnYiJ9LCJwdXIiOiJ2YXJpYXRpb24ifX0=--21f3793904e6ce1806a5a794a691217fceef82c7/bah.jpg" alt="Episode artwork: Smoked Hams, Sunny Escapes, and Holiday Tales" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>From snowy Michigan to sunny Florida, the guys share their holiday escapades — navigating climate
    shocks and a first-ever Thanksgiving experiment with a pellet smoker. Michael's smoked ham wins the
    family over, while Adam's household chuckles over their less-meaty lifestyle.</p>
    <p>It's a festive one, sprinkled with humor and warmth, and they take time to celebrate the leisure
    community and shine the Listener Spotlight on another town where fans are tuning in.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/16238805">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E25 · November 24, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/16148905">Gift Ideas, Wheels, Whiskey, and Holiday Cheer</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6MTM1NDQzMTM0LCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--b1548e3757d685dc7e439d16eb946dc4c2821c9a/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJqcGciLCJyZXNpemVfdG9fZmlsbCI6WzI1MCwyNTAseyJjcm9wIjoiY2VudHJlIn1dLCJzYXZlciI6eyJxdWFsaXR5Ijo2MH0sImNvbG91cnNwYWNlIjoic3JnYiJ9LCJwdXIiOiJ2YXJpYXRpb24ifX0=--21f3793904e6ce1806a5a794a691217fceef82c7/xmas.jpg" alt="Episode artwork: Gift Ideas, Wheels, Whiskey, and Holiday Cheer" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>A heartwarming one: the guys share a touching Veterans Day celebration, including a surprise steak
    dinner for Adam's veteran father — a reminder of the importance of gratitude.</p>
    <p>From there they dive into community updates and roll into the holiday season with cycling gift ideas,
    a little whiskey talk, and plenty of good cheer.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/16148905">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E24 · November 10, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/16046948">Pedals, Pagosa, and Cycling Camaraderie: A Journey of Adventures and Festive Wishes</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6MTM0NDk2ODQ0LCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--9afcc73ed7558436c448f017997cd68411892580/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJqcGciLCJyZXNpemVfdG9fZmlsbCI6WzI1MCwyNTAseyJjcm9wIjoiY2VudHJlIn1dLCJzYXZlciI6eyJxdWFsaXR5Ijo2MH0sImNvbG91cnNwYWNlIjoic3JnYiJ9LCJwdXIiOiJ2YXJpYXRpb24ifX0=--21f3793904e6ce1806a5a794a691217fceef82c7/IG.png" alt="Episode artwork: Pedals, Pagosa, and Cycling Camaraderie" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>The journey rivals the destination in this one. The guys open with a playful cycling-gear debate and
    the lingering suspense over the new president's identity (still unknown when they recorded), champion
    small businesses, and find the natural solidarity that biking fosters.</p>
    <p>They spin into "Our Leisure Community," spotlighting listener stories and global connections from New
    Zealand to Kenya — with Maria Parker's awe-inspiring journey stealing the show and admiration from fans
    like Keith, Luke, and Scott. Then a scenic detour through Pagosa Springs, Colorado, from Wolf Creek
    skiing to riverboat-casino tales and local legends.</p>
    <p>As the festive season nears, they tee up the Cycling Christmas Wish List segment, share indoor-cycling
    tips, uncover the Swiss roots of a historic community, and toast the growing influence of women in the
    whiskey industry.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/16046948">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E23 · October 27, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/15971860">Spooky Pedals and Paranormal Tales: A Halloween Cycling Adventure with Adam and Michael</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6MTMzMzE2ODY4LCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--350dd76e8aff99efbd43815dc83c7c35062562f1/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJqcGciLCJyZXNpemVfdG9fZmlsbCI6WzI1MCwyNTAseyJjcm9wIjoiY2VudHJlIn1dLCJzYXZlciI6eyJxdWFsaXR5Ijo2MH0sImNvbG91cnNwYWNlIjoic3JnYiJ9LCJwdXIiOiJ2YXJpYXRpb24ifX0=--21f3793904e6ce1806a5a794a691217fceef82c7/HCover.jpg" alt="Episode artwork: Spooky Pedals and Paranormal Tales" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>A Halloween-themed ride packed with spooky tales and cycling mishaps. The guys share a listener's
    thrilling car encounter in southern Minnesota, get into the festive spirit with playful mask banter, and
    introduce a bourbon as mysterious as a werewolf's howl — Moonlight Mayhem.</p>
    <p>They celebrate the community with heartwarming stories — Adam and Kelly marking their anniversary in
    CMOL t-shirts, the quirky world of DeBrim hats — and turn the City Spotlight on Columbus, Ohio, with a
    guessing game to stump the quizmasters.</p>
    <p>Balancing humor with reflection, they confront the sobering topic of ghost bikes and road safety
    before lightening the mood with a comical top-10 list of cycling fears — from Strava hacks to mud
    mishaps — and speculate on the coming RAGBRAI-52 logo reveal.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/15971860">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E22 · October 13, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/15891264">Hurricanes, Hope, and Two-Wheeled Tales — Cycling Women of Leisure Series with Maria Parker</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6MTMyNDE4NTUwLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--4d25a80de1c7a5e4ee35b0cf74e55d54be070af8/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJqcGciLCJyZXNpemVfdG9fZmlsbCI6WzI1MCwyNTAseyJjcm9wIjoiY2VudHJlIn1dLCJzYXZlciI6eyJxdWFsaXR5Ijo2MH0sImNvbG91cnNwYWNlIjoic3JnYiJ9LCJwdXIiOiJ2YXJpYXRpb24ifX0=--21f3793904e6ce1806a5a794a691217fceef82c7/Maria%20P.png" alt="Episode artwork: Hurricanes, Hope, and Two-Wheeled Tales with Maria Parker" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>A leisure trip to Florida turns into an unexpected adventure when a family illness and looming
    hurricanes prompt an early return. Amid lighthearted quips, the guys share community feedback, shout out
    Gary Vaughn and Matt Robinson, and — inspired by a close call with a vehicle — launch a new segment,
    "Encounters with Cars."</p>
    <p>A scenic detour relives the Tour de Livingston event in Michigan before the spotlight turns to Maria
    Parker, CEO of Cruise Bike, who shares the benefits of their front-wheel-drive aerocycles and her
    incredible Race Across America journey.</p>
    <p>The conversation deepens into Maria's fundraising for brain-cancer research — motivated by her sister
    Jenny's battle with glioblastoma — and the 3,000 Miles to a Cure initiative, closing on the growing
    inclusivity that e-bikes bring to the sport.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/15891264">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E21 · September 29, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/15764507">From Flat Tires to High Fives: A Cycling Journey</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6MTMxMDM4NTE5LCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--6622af95b39d5fff5f5df63601775d4dfa59167e/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJqcGciLCJyZXNpemVfdG9fZmlsbCI6WzI1MCwyNTAseyJjcm9wIjoiY2VudHJlIn1dLCJzYXZlciI6eyJxdWFsaXR5Ijo2MH0sImNvbG91cnNwYWNlIjoic3JnYiJ9LCJwdXIiOiJ2YXJpYXRpb24ifX0=--21f3793904e6ce1806a5a794a691217fceef82c7/CWOL%203.jpg" alt="Episode artwork: From Flat Tires to High Fives" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>Between a bustling week and a packed agenda, the guys still find time for the community. They
    celebrate their very first subscriber, Scott (and ponder sending him some swag), debut a new fan-mail
    feature with a listener question from Overland Park, Kansas about the time it takes to make the podcast,
    and sprinkle in banter about local spots and Starbucks orders.</p>
    <p>The City Spotlight shouts out Ed — who listens at 1.6x speed — and the loyal listeners in Overland
    Park, with jerseys now spotted at events in British Columbia and Tennessee, plus a teaser about an
    intriguing upcoming spotlight guest.</p>
    <p>Then they relive the hilliest RAGBRAI route in its 51-year history — fully loaded touring bikes,
    camaraderie and hospitality, flat tires and mechanical mishaps, a nostalgic visit to the American Gothic
    House, and a chance run-in with their Jack Rue sales rep at the expo.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/15764507">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E20 · September 15, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/15750277">Milestones, Memories, and Two-Wheeled Triumphs: Celebrating Our 50th Episode</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6MTMwOTA4MzMyLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--0e44e93b9c8455b185cc1c929f5dd583a0ff7492/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJqcGciLCJyZXNpemVfdG9fZmlsbCI6WzI1MCwyNTAseyJjcm9wIjoiY2VudHJlIn1dLCJzYXZlciI6eyJxdWFsaXR5Ijo2MH0sImNvbG91cnNwYWNlIjoic3JnYiJ9LCJwdXIiOiJ2YXJpYXRpb24ifX0=--21f3793904e6ce1806a5a794a691217fceef82c7/50th%20Show.jpg" alt="Episode artwork: Celebrating Our 50th Episode" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>A milestone celebration: the guys mark their 50th episode. Michael flips the script to handle the
    intro as they reflect on the journey — surpassing 10,000 downloads on Buzzsprout, connecting with a
    global audience, and all the friendships made along the way.</p>
    <p>They pull back the curtain on what goes into each episode, from hiring their beloved voiceover artist
    "NASA Girl" to chasing mysterious sound issues, and share how they've embraced imperfection and
    conversational flow — plus their idea for concise "Snapcasts."</p>
    <p>They also announce the return of the "Cycling Women of Leisure" series, debate aluminum versus carbon
    fiber wheelsets, tour the history of Waxhaw, and riff on work-from-home Zoom meetings.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/15750277">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E19 · September 1, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/15654228">Cycling Adventures, Historic Tales, and Mackinac Memories: A Shoreline Recap</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6MTI5NzA2MDM1LCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--c61c6c1e52ad8634183a2e34f6ee31c59aa4b9c0/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJqcGciLCJyZXNpemVfdG9fZmlsbCI6WzI1MCwyNTAseyJjcm9wIjoiY2VudHJlIn1dLCJzYXZlciI6eyJxdWFsaXR5Ijo2MH0sImNvbG91cnNwYWNlIjoic3JnYiJ9LCJwdXIiOiJ2YXJpYXRpb24ifX0=--21f3793904e6ce1806a5a794a691217fceef82c7/Mightymac.jpg" alt="Episode artwork: Shoreline Recap — Mackinac Memories" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>Part two of the Shoreline Recap opens with a touching chat about Michael's daughter Miya heading into
    eighth grade, then journeys to Beltsville, Maryland to uncover its historical roots — and a bit of
    cryptid lore.</p>
    <p>There's an out-loud-funny shopping escapade in Mackinac City involving a ceramic ornament, a
    good-humored store clerk, and a playful fudge-shop prank on Jess. From there they roll the scenic route
    from Mackinac City to Charlevoix, soaking in the Tunnel of Trees and charming towns like Elk Rapids and
    Petoskey.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/15654228">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
