    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6Njc4MDA3NTAsInB1ciI6ImJsb2JfaWQifX0=----2454c883dcd12a10059f243d8ea753f8b5c1613e/CML%20Road%20Adventures%20Cover%20Art.jpg" alt="Episode artwork: Spokes and Sports — Route Revelations" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>Riding the high of Michigan's national-championship season, Adam and Michael look back on the
    friendly ribbing between rival teams and the camaraderie that sports bring — with a nod to Franklin,
    whose New Year's route reveal was as dazzling as the fireworks. They take listeners behind the scenes
    of the big BRAG 2024 route announcement and the secrecy they were sworn to keep.</p>
    <p>Then it's a cross-country journey through memory lane, weighing a slate of possible rides now that
    the guys are sitting out RAGBRAI this year — from BRAN and Tour de Nebraska to BAK's 50th anniversary,
    Cycle Zydeco in Louisiana, Ride the Fault Line, OATBRAN in Nevada, and the newly re-routed Ride
    Shoreline in Michigan. Schedules are a jigsaw puzzle, but the wish list keeps growing.</p>
    <p>Along the way they trade stories of headwinds and hills, ponder the logistics of flying with a bike,
    and connect over a shared love of aviation — open roads and open skies, just a play button away.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/14283397">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E2 · January 7, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/14245286">Rolling Past Antebellum Elegance: BIG BRAG 2024 Route In-Depth Preview with Franklin Johnson</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6MTA2MTA3MzEwLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19----2454c883dcd12a10059f243d8ea753f8b5c1613e/IMG_1342.JPG" alt="Episode artwork: BIG BRAG 2024 Route Preview with Franklin Johnson" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>Still buzzing from the New Year's fireworks, Michael and Adam recount the celebration that launched
    planning for their most ambitious escapade yet: BIG BRAG 2024 from Atlanta to Savannah. Franklin Johnson
    drops by with a cyclist's treasure map, tracing a route full of historical gems and Southern splendor —
    from Oglethorpe University's starting line to the cobblestones of River Street — and calls on all free
    spirits to join the Cycling Men of Leisure team.</p>
    <p>Along the way they take detours into Georgia's quaint towns, where college quads and Hollywood tales
    abound. Oxford's academic charm gives way to Milledgeville's antebellum pride and its complicated
    embrace of the new Rivian plant, with talk of a Milledgeville concert and the traditional bandana earned
    after a grueling century ride. They wheel from Statesboro's blues to one local festival after the next.</p>
    <p>As the journey nears its end, the allure of Savannah's Spanish moss becomes irresistible — trading
    bikes for a leisurely stroll through the city's historic squares. Every twist in the route unfolds a new
    chapter of camaraderie and discovery.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/14245286">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="post">
    <div class="meta">S3E1 · January 1, 2024</div>
    <h3><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/14194597-georgia-on-two-wheels-unveiling-the-brag-2024-cycling-route-with-franklin-johnson">Georgia on Two Wheels: Unveiling the BRAG 2024 Cycling Route with Franklin Johnson</a></h3>
    <img class="art" src="https://www.buzzsprout.com/rails/active_storage/representations/redirect/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsiZGF0YSI6Njc4MDA3NTAsInB1ciI6ImJsb2JfaWQifX0=----2454c883dcd12a10059f243d8ea753f8b5c1613e/CML%20Road%20Adventures%20Cover%20Art.jpg" alt="Episode artwork: Unveiling the BRAG 2024 Cycling Route with Franklin Johnson" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <p>As the clock ticks closer to BIG BRAG 2024, Michael and Adam are joined by special guest Franklin
    Johnson to celebrate the newly announced route from Atlanta to Savannah. Feel the past come alive
    beneath your wheels as they pedal through Georgia's picturesque towns, each with a story to tell.</p>
    <p>With his usual charisma, Franklin reveals the route's nod to a historic military march and bubbles
    over about the special layover day in Milledgeville — a town with a charm you have to experience to
    believe. Every turn of the pedal is a brush with history, a ride through nature's canvases, and a
    visit to the quaintest of Southern towns.</p>
    <p>They recount the allure of Covington and Oxford, where movie magic meets the streets, and the
    familiar touch of Social Circle, a place close to Franklin's heart — before that well-earned midweek
    breather in Milledgeville, with local distillery tours and the simple pleasure of catching up on
    laundry.</p>
    <p class="listen"><a href="https://www.cyclingmenofleisurepodcast.com/2054444/episodes/14194597-georgia-on-two-wheels-unveiling-the-brag-2024-cycling-route-with-franklin-johnson">Listen to the episode →</a></p>
  </article>

